+### Framework defaults adopted (Rails 7.1 and 7.2)
+
+Reviewed and adopted, beyond the message defaults of decision 1:
+
+* `action_view.sanitizer_vendor = Rails::HTML5::Sanitizer`: Redmine's wiki
+  formatting has its own sanitizers. The only core use that depended on it,
+  heading anchors, now pins the HTML4 sanitizer (see "What changed").
+* `dom_testing_default_html_version = :html5` (tests only; one test fixed).
+* `active_record.sqlite3_adapter_strict_strings_by_default`: SQLite rejects
+  double-quoted string literals. The suite and all 310 migrations from scratch
+  (`rake db:migrate redmine:load_default_data` on an empty database, what CI's
+  `ci:setup` does) pass on SQLite. Plugins with such raw SQL fail on SQLite.
+* `add_autoload_paths_to_load_path = false`: `app/*` directories are no longer
+  in `$LOAD_PATH`. Redmine uses autoloading (and `lib/` is still in
+  `$LOAD_PATH`); plugins that `require` files of `app/` must use autoloading.
+* `active_record.postgresql_adapter_decode_dates`: only raw `select_*` results
+  change (dates instead of strings); Redmine selects no raw dates and its
+  grouped counts were already typed by the result's column types.
+* `active_support.raise_on_invalid_cache_expiration_time`: Redmine only uses
+  `expires_in: 30.days`.
+* `active_record.validate_migration_timestamps`: only rejects versions more
+  than a day in the future (plugin migrations named `001_...` are fine).
+* `precompile_filter_parameters`, `active_record.raise_on_assign_to_attr_readonly`
+  (no `attr_readonly`), `generate_secure_token_on` (no `has_secure_token`),
+  `before_committed_on_all_records`, `belongs_to_required_validates_foreign_key`
+  (moot), `query_log_tags_format` (query logs off), the Active Record
+  encryption defaults (not used), `debug_exception_log_level = :error`,
+  `log_file_size` (development and test).
+* `action_dispatch.default_headers` without `X-Download-Options: noopen`
+  (Internet Explorer 8 only), see the ops notes.
 
