+   `Redmine::RollbackCompatibility`) is **not** a rollback override and must
+   not be retired blindly: a user whose session cookie dates from Rails 6.1 is
+   signed out without it (verified). Redmine refreshes a session token
+   (`tokens`, `action = 'session'`) at least every minute it is used, and
+   every request since the Rails 7.0 deployment rewrote the cookie in the
+   current format. So retire them only if, with `redmine_verify_sessions` on
+   (the default), no session token was last used before the Rails 7.0
+   deployment:
