+   Otherwise keep them (Rails 8.1 supports them, they cost nothing). With
+   them, `:json` would be the only change, and it writes the same JSON.
+   The SHA1 verifier rotations can go once 30 days have passed since the
+   last mail sent by Rails 6.1 (ie. 30 days after the Rails 7.0 deployment,
+   or after the last rollback to Rails 6.1).
+4. Keep `Redmine::RollbackCompatibility.keep_secret_key_base` until ops have
+   moved the secret to a single source (no "secrets.yml" warning in the logs,
